+++ b/README.md
@@ -31,6 +31,57 @@ docker run -d --restart=always -e RUNTIME_PREFIX="Kit-" -e RUNTIME_NAME="MyRunti
 
 Video instruction: [https://youtu.be/HQrsGY7XLU4](https://youtu.be/HQrsGY7XLU4)
 
+### Raspberry Pi ARM64 With External Broker
+
+Build the ARM64 runtime image from this directory and export it for Podman:
+
+```bash
+docker buildx build --builder default --platform linux/arm64 --load \
+	-t sdv-runtime:mw-com .
+docker save -o sdv-runtime-mw-com.tar sdv-runtime:mw-com
+```
+
+Copy the archive to the Pi/QEMU guest, then load and run it there:
+
+```bash
+podman load -i /tmp/sdv-runtime-mw-com.tar
+podman run -d --replace --pull=never --name sdv-runtime-pi \
+	-p 127.0.0.1:3202:3090 \
+	-e KUKSA_DATABROKER_HOST=host.containers.internal \
+	-e KUKSA_DATABROKER_PORT=55555 \
+	-e RUNTIME_NAME=RaspberryPi-Python \
+	docker.io/library/sdv-runtime:mw-com
+```
+
+The ARM64 and AMD64 images disable their bundled databroker and mock provider by default;
+the Python syncer and Kit Manager still start. The syncer connects to the
+databroker running on the guest at port 55555. Ensure that broker is listening
+on a guest interface reachable from the Podman container. The Kit Manager is
+available on the guest at `127.0.0.1:3202`.
+
+### Playground signal writes without mocks
+
+Widget `write_signals_value` requests publish broker **current values** for all
+registered writable entry types, including actuators. With `MOCK_SIGNAL=""`,
+Signal Watch `set_mock_signals` requests also publish current values directly;
+neither subscribing nor setting values starts a mock provider. CLI `get` and
+playground subscriptions read those same current values. Configured real vehicle
+feedback can subsequently replace them.
+
+The external mw::com broker forwards published current values for configured
+command-capable mappings through middleware. Sensor-only entries are not sent as
+commands. Unknown paths, invalid values, and denied writes return a `Failed`
+reply with an `error`, rather than a successful acknowledgement.
+
+When `MOCK_SIGNAL` names a file, `set_mock_signals` retains its mock-configuration
+behavior. Native CLI `actuate` remains a separate actuator-target operation.
+
+Run the write-path regression tests in an environment with the runtime dependencies:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s test -p test_signal_writes.py
+```
+
 ### Arguments for setting runtime name
 `$RUNTIME_NAME`: this is the ID to add your runtime to playground.digital.auto.
 `$RUNTIME_PREFIX`: (Optional) Custom prefix for the runtime ID. Default is "Runtime-". Set to empty string for no prefix.
